WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.470
Switch on a lamp, and it glows.

2
00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:05.190
Leave it on, and it keeps on glowing.

3
00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:08.590
So does the lamp use up the
current that flows through it?

4
00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:12.530
Here is a simple circuit: a
cell, some wires and a lamp,

5
00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:14.690
joined in one loop.

6
00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:16.430
Charge starts to flow.

7
00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:19.030
Now put an ammeter in
the loop before the lamp,

8
00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:20.730
and another one after it.

9
00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:23.170
Will the second ammeter read less?

10
00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:25.390
In this mission, you'll meet current,

11
00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:27.710
potential difference and resistance.

12
00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:31.150
Then you'll compare series
and parallel circuits.

13
00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:35.230
Your mission: find out whether
a lamp uses up current.
